# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 (a `for` row per child, keyed; widget recursion over the data) and ch. 7 (R7: a row is built at the end of the tick its key arrives): "b" is the root's row 0, and the click gives "b" a row of its own, "c".
test the_outline_grows_a_level

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="grow")
    1: Ui.Label(text="a")
    2/[0]/0: Ui.Label(text="b")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  added:
    2/[0]/1/[0]/0: Ui.Label(text="c")
